@rendermode InteractiveServer
@implements IDisposable
@inject AuthenticationStateProvider AuthProvider
@inject NavigationManager Nav

@* Renders nothing. Its job is to hold a live circuit on every admin page and act the moment
   AdminRevalidatingAuthenticationStateProvider decides the signed-in account is no longer valid —
   deactivated, demoted (FR-104) or deleted — by navigating the browser out to /login.

   Why a component in the LAYOUT rather than <AuthorizeRouteView> in the router: this app renders the
   router and the layout as static SSR and marks individual pages @rendermode InteractiveServer. The
   router's NotAuthorized content is documented as inoperative under static SSR, so the redirect
   cannot live there — tried, and the E2E test sat happily on /bokningar after the account was
   deactivated. An interactive island inside the static layout is present on every admin page and
   shares that page's circuit, which is where the revalidation runs.

   The framework's own response to a failed revalidation is only to swap the circuit's principal for
   an anonymous one (RevalidatingServerAuthenticationStateProvider.ForceSignOut). Nothing navigates,
   and with a static router the [Authorize] attributes are not re-evaluated in an open tab — so
   without this component the tab keeps working until someone reloads it.

   forceLoad: a full navigation, so the request re-runs cookie authentication (whose own check is on
   the same interval) and the dead circuit is abandoned rather than reused. *@

@code {
    protected override void OnInitialized() =>
        AuthProvider.AuthenticationStateChanged += OnAuthenticationStateChanged;

    private void OnAuthenticationStateChanged(Task<AuthenticationState> task) => _ = HandleAsync(task);

    private async Task HandleAsync(Task<AuthenticationState> task)
    {
        var state = await task;
        if (state.User.Identity?.IsAuthenticated == true)
            return;

        // InvokeAsync: the notification arrives on the revalidation loop's thread, not the circuit's.
        await InvokeAsync(() => Nav.NavigateTo("/login", forceLoad: true));
    }

    public void Dispose() => AuthProvider.AuthenticationStateChanged -= OnAuthenticationStateChanged;
}
